{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'clojure-callsite|yang.clojure|def included|def probe-order|check-manifest' src/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"src/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj:53:(def probe-order\nsrc/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj:100:   \"yang.clojure\" \"yang.safepoint\" \"yang.python.antlr.uast\"\nsrc/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj:243:(def included\nsrc/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj:286:   ;; made check-manifest! refuse every lane mode; 17 tests, 57 assertions,\nsrc/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj:353:(defn check-manifest!\nsrc/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj:765:        (println \"J2 manifest OK:\" (pr-str (check-manifest! \"test\" included excluded)))\ntest/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc:1:(ns yang.clojure-callsite-test\ntest/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc:2:  \"Contract C1 for production yang.clojure (Addendum A, design §2): the\ntest/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc:16:            [yang.clojure :as yang]\ntest/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc:17:            [yang.clojure.prelude :as clj-prelude]\ntest/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc:152:    (let [ast yang.clojure.prelude/module-uast\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n '\"'^## |''^### |5'\"\\\\.2|5\\\\.3|6\\\\.1|6\\\\.2|6\\\\.3' collab/yang-clojure/1794670000000-architect-callsite-generalization-design.gpt-6-astra.findings.md\"","aggregated_output":"10:## 1. Decision and evidence limits\n20:### 1.1 The oracle format is not yet available to freeze\n22:The inspected worktree `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-aaq`, branch `attribution-as-query`, reports HEAD `3eebe844e406ba56bc38a5f4b4a0098d811b5efd`. Its tracked `test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:1794-1839` still generates two-field body-entry traces and uses the offset accounting at lines 1786–1819. Its `BRIEF-aaq.md:15-21` requires the future inventory, three-field instrumentation, and versioned mechanically derived site tables; it does not define their schema. Untracked `probe/aaq_probe.clj:17-29` uses exploratory map-key paths, not the canonical row-position paths; it is not a published contract. The local dispatch log `collab/yang-clojure/1794630000000-engineer-attribution-as-query.glm-5.3.stdout.log:1` reports an unrecognized-model error. This does not establish the status of work elsewhere.\n28:## 2. Occurrence contract C1\n32:### 2.1 Identity and scope\n47:### 2.2 Minimal persisted annotation\n63:### 2.3 Finalization and transformations\n71:### 2.4 Lowering, reconstruction, and runtime lookup\n73:Persist the existing instruction relation `[segment-address pc origin root-address path]`. The row linearizer already returns `{:address ... :provenance [[pc origin root path] ...]}`; its caller supplies the segment coordinate (`semantic/linearize.cljc:188-214`; code-as-tuples §5.3 at lines 918–931). A call dispatch looks up its **own call instruction's** emitting occurrence, not the preceding operand's instruction or the callee's body. Multiple instructions may belong to one occurrence.\n79:### 2.5 Ephemeral origin and trace field\n103:## 3. A2 inventory: revisions, preservation, and refusal\n107:### 3.1 Contract revision decisions\n128:### 3.2 Producer-to-consumer preservation inventory\n155:### 3.3 Persisted artifacts and publication blast radius\n170:### 3.4 Failure separation\n176:## 4. R1 durable correspondence schema D1\n178:### 4.1 Additive envelope\n221:### 4.2 Independent reconstruction and discovery\n239:## 5. A3 adoption briefs and ordering\n245:### 5.1 Mandatory host sets\n260:### 5.2 Cross-host equality without collapsing admissions\n274:### 5.3 Frontend-specific work packages\n286:## 6. Measurement and declared budgets\n290:### 6.1 Counts and cost model\n302:### 6.2 Experiment separation\n314:### 6.3 Bounds published before any tagged run\n331:### 6.4 Budget impact allocated per frontend\n342:## 7. Correctness and refusal gates\n365:## 8. Acceptance sequence and owner risks\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'jolt|shiva|jupiter|ssh|overlap' docs/agents/build-n-test.md | tail -65\"","aggregated_output":"34:# which lanes may overlap.\n53:# G2 changed sets, full suites, slow tier, nightly) run on shiva/jupiter --\n64:# overlap lanes, see \"Remote test servers\" below).\n127:`test:sub`. As in the shiva script below, currently unowned namespaces run\n205:jupiter 5,645 s at 12 workers, shiva comparable). Do not run another lane\n231:does not make overlapping builds and tests safe. Peer executables and shadow\n394:  disjoint lane pair (`src/dev/nightly.clj`): **jupiter takes the jvm lane, shiva\n395:  takes node and dart** (each lane in its own clone; shiva publishes the run pin,\n396:  jupiter reads it and falls back to its own current master as an advisory run).\n413:| Full JVM lane, one process, before tagging (shiva) | 70 min |\n414:| Full JVM lane, sharded by subsystem, before tagging (jupiter, 13 shards, 8 at a time) | 46.5 min, set by `yin.repl.python-antlr-test` |\n415:| **Quick tier, sharded by subsystem (jupiter, same 13 shards)** | **5 min 3 s**, 4055 tests, all shards exit 0; longest shards `yang.python` 253 s and `yin.vm.ucf` 204 s |\n416:| **Slow tier (shiva, one JVM per namespace, 6 at a time)** | **53 min**, 22 namespaces, 168 tests, all exit 0; longest `yin.repl.python-antlr-test` 3183 s (about 1580 s alone on the laptop) |\n502:## Remote test servers: shiva and jupiter\n510:| `shiva.stigmergy.systems` | 24 / 62 GB | Server snapshot: java 21, clojure 1.12.4.1602, node 25.6.1, babashka, cljstyle, zprint, flutter 3.47.1. The repo's `mise.toml` selects Flutter `latest` on beta, not a fixed version. Activate the repo toolchain before running any lane. |\n511:| `jupiter.stigmergy.systems` | 48 / 62 GB | Server snapshot (rechecked 2026-10-29): java 21, clojure 1.12.4.1602, node 25.6.1, babashka, cljstyle, zprint, flutter 3.47.8 (the stale hand-symlinked 3.41.9 was replaced via `mise install flutter@3.47.8` after it failed to compile `dart:ui`-using cljd namespaces; if the Dart lane dies in the cljd compile, check `mise ls flutter` first). mise was moved off the apt package to the official user-local install (`~/.local/bin/mise`, 2026.11.2, owner action 2026-11-07) so both hosts share shiva's layout; toolchains in `~/.local/share/mise/installs/` were untouched. Tri-host quick tier verified green on 2026-10-29 (see Measured times). |\n515:shiva and jupiter are **peers**, not a primary and a spare (owner ruling\n516:2026-11-15, superseding the earlier \"leave jupiter out, use shiva\" routing).\n517:jupiter has the larger core budget (48 vs 24). Before dispatching any\n523:for h in shiva.stigmergy.systems jupiter.stigmergy.systems; do\n524:  echo \"== $h\"; ssh \"$h\" uptime\n530:work. If the loads are comparable, prefer jupiter (more cores). Two\n532:keeps jupiter=JVM / shiva=node+dart because the lanes are sharded and\n539:that is behind origin (shiva: 45 commits behind on 2026-10-11) and belongs to its\n548:(yang.php branch-tip gate, jupiter): the yang.php lane failed with\n601:ssh shiva.stigmergy.systems 'set -e; mkdir -p ~/ci; cd ~/workspace/datomworld;\n616:refs. Measured on shiva 2026-11-02: the `dg` clone was created from the `p4`\n640:A non-interactive `ssh host cmd` does not load the shell profile, so `mise` and its\n645:export PATH=\"$HOME/.local/bin:/snap/bin:$PATH\"   # mise: ~/.local/bin on shiva, /snap/bin on jupiter\n657:### Which lanes may overlap (reconciling the one-lane-set rule)\n664:average over 100 on 2026-11-01; the remote hosts own that tier. On shiva (24 cores) and jupiter (48) the cores are not the limit, so\n665:lanes may overlap, with these limits:\n672:  gives the Dart lane its own copies, so the two lanes then overlap safely. This is\n681:- Do not treat this as permission to overlap lanes on the laptop.\n683:The first run on shiva (2026-10-11) overlapped JVM and Dart in one clone before\n695:join. A single-lane invocation (jupiter's `jvm`) is unchanged: one clone,\n697:command line (shiva: `node,dart` + `--pin-publish`; jupiter: `jvm` +\n698:`--pin-read --pin-peer shiva...`) is the only difference.\n707:   the measured miss on shiva 2026-11-02: the cljs lane ran but the\n761:### The jolt J2 lane: run it with `--jobs` on the servers\n763:The jolt lane's core mode (`bb src/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj core [--jobs N]\n764:[--only re] [--timeout-ms M]`) runs each test namespace as its own child jolt\n767:only thing `--jobs N` overlaps is the waiting. The default is `jobs 1`\n768:(strictly serial), which on jupiter makes the full ~179-namespace lane a\n773:- jolt children are essentially single-threaded (the 16 MiB parse thread\n775:  sit far inside jupiter's 48 cores / 62 GB and shiva's 24 / 62;\n779:  `step-timeout-ms` in `src/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj`), so beyond ~16 workers\n834:ssh <host> 'tmux new-session -d -s ci-full \"bash -lc \\\"~/ci/run-full.sh ~/ci/datomworld-<name> ~/ci/datomworld-<name>-dart > ~/ci/run-full.out 2>&1\\\"\"'\n837:Watch it: `ssh <host>`, then `tmux attach -t ci-full` (detach with `Ctrl-b d`; do not\n859:  on shiva: the namespace passes 5/5.\n862:- Both hosts run other work (a QEMU guest and rustdesk on shiva); idle load is\n876:  shiva and jupiter, hourly cron plus a 04:00 Vietnam guard and flock,\n879:  the JVM full suite on jupiter, the full Node and Dart suites on shiva.\n919:First full tri-host verification of jupiter. Prerequisites (npm ci, Node REPL,\n924:laptop — route Node lanes to shiva; the laptop comparison is historical and\n929:taken-port/bind-failed signature recorded above). Routing summary: jupiter\n943:### Remote agent execution (delegate CLIs on shiva and jupiter)\n980:Known state: `claude` and `codex` verified working on shiva (2026-10-24, the\n981:jolt canonical-fixes verification ran there); `glm` reported available by the\n983:the full tri-host suite (jupiter verified 2026-10-29 — see Measured times;\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
