ained admitted syntax keeps its own admission's source origin\")\n731:        (is (empty? (filter second-origins first-origins))\n732:            \"the two admissions' occurrence origins are disjoint — the\n734:        (is (not= first-origins second-origins)\n735:            \"not the input's source origin: each admission's rows carry\n736:             that admission's own origins\")\n738:                [[\"first\" first-tree first-origin]\n739:                 [\"second\" second-tree second-origin]]]\n740:          (let [rows (macro/call-site-table consumer tree admission)\n741:                final (macro/packet->row-set tree)]\n745:                         {:declared? true :per-occurrence-origins? true}))\n752:    (let [store (macro/seed-store\n753:                  (macro/make-ctx {:token :callsite-test/standard-forms\n755:                  [macro/stdlib-forms])\n756:          ctx (macro/make-ctx {:token \"callsite-test\"\n763:          first-origin [:source :program-in (:t ctx) 0]\n764:          consumer (macro/make-expander ctx nil)\n765:          consumer (macro/load consumer (encoder/program-batch claimed))\n767:          second-origin [:source :program-in (:t (:ctx consumer)) 0]\n768:          consumer (macro/load consumer (encoder/program-batch unmarked))\n772:      (is (seq (macro/call-site-table consumer first-tree first-origin))\n773:          \"the claimed occurrence's table is still held under its origin\")\n774:      (is (nil? (macro/call-site-table consumer second-tree second-origin))\n813:    (let [store (macro/seed-store\n814:                  (macro/make-ctx {:token :callsite-test/standard-forms\n816:                  [macro/stdlib-forms])\n817:          ctx (macro/make-ctx {:token \"callsite-test\"\n826:            (macro/expand-batch batch ctx)]\n833:              (macro/expand-batch batch ctx)]\n838:(deftest publish-version-reason-test\n848:              res (publish/publish-module!\n856:          (is (= :yin.link.publish/unsupported-call-sit